From 1b65c2b790b3ac7590a80fa20cb3e1680d3030bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Use the paid tier properly: best model first, AI runs
 automatically

The $5 prepaid credit moves the key from 20 requests per day per model to
10,000, so the decisions that were made to protect a tiny free quota are now
the wrong ones.

* Model chain is ordered best-first instead of cheapest-first. Budget is no
  longer the constraint, so the chain now exists for resilience (a model
  briefly 503s, or is retired) rather than to add four small allowances
  together. Dropped gemini-2.5-flash-lite, which was failing silently.

* The problem detail page now asks the AI by itself instead of showing a
  button. Word overlap still renders first so the page is never blank, then
  the AI answer replaces it. Making the user click for the headline feature
  only made sense when each click cost 5% of the day's quota.

* A timeout no longer abandons the whole chain. Previously the first model
  timing out returned None immediately and models 2-4 were never tried.

* Added a whole-request deadline (AI_DEADLINE, 45s) so no combination of
  slow providers can hang a user's request.

* Added a dormant second provider (Groq), active only if GROQ_API_KEY is set.
  With it unset the module behaves exactly as a Gemini-only client, which is
  what the manuscript describes. It is insurance against prepaid credit
  running out mid-demonstration.

* check_gemini.py now probes both providers and prints the exact status per
  model, so a retired model name is distinguishable from a spent quota.

Verified: 32/32 smoke checks, 21/21 provider-chain checks (success, 429
fallthrough, timeout recovery, garbage replies, cache), frontend builds.

