+"""The AI layer of Solution Matching: re-ranking.
+
+TF-IDF gathers plausible candidates cheaply. This module asks a language model
+which of them are actually about the same underlying problem, and why - the
+part word-overlap cannot do, because "street light is out" and "walang ilaw sa
+kanto" share no words at all.
+
+PROVIDERS
+---------
+Gemini is the provider. It is named in the manuscript, it is tried first, and
+on a paid tier key it is the only one that ever runs.
+
+A second provider (Groq) is supported but DORMANT: it activates only if
+GROQ_API_KEY is present in .env, and only after every Gemini model has
+refused with 429. Leave GROQ_API_KEY unset and this module behaves exactly as
+a Gemini-only client - which is what the manuscript describes.
+
+It is here as insurance. Billing on this project is prepaid credit, and credit
+can run out at an inconvenient moment; a demonstration that falls back to a
+second provider is better than one that falls back to nothing. If you would
+rather not have to explain it at defense, deleting the Groq adapter below and
+the "groq" entry in _active_providers() removes it completely.
+
+DESIGN RULES, all deliberate
+----------------------------
+* **Optional.** Unlike Services/email.py, missing API keys do NOT raise at
+  import. The app must run without any key, falling back to TF-IDF alone.
 * **Never fatal.** Any failure - no key, timeout, quota, malformed reply -
   returns None. The caller then uses the TF-IDF result it already has.
-* **One call per search**, not per problem, so the free quota survives a week
-  of user testing.
-* Gemini's reply is treated as *data*, never as instructions.
+* **One call per search**, not per problem, so the free quota lasts.
+* **Bounded.** The whole re-rank gives up after AI_DEADLINE seconds no matter
+  how many providers and models are left, so a slow provider can never hang
+  a user's request.
+* The model's reply is treated as *data*, never as instructions.
 
